{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 18:05:49 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_tool_output_refinement] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunks\": [{\"byte_end\": 5835, \"byte_start\": 0, \"chunk_index\": 0, \"content\": \"# Implementation Report: Stages 1-3 - Session Isolation Feature\\n**Date**: 2026-01-03\\n**Agent**: CoderAgent\\n**Project**: scribe_tool_output_refinement\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nSuccessfully implemented session-aware reminder hash generation feature across three stages, enabling isolated reminder deduplication per agent session while maintaining full backward compatibility.\\n\\n**Status**: \\u2705 Complete\\n**Test Results**: 32/32 passing (5 new tests + 27 existing tests)\\n**Confidence**: 0.95\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scope of Work\\n\\n### Stage 1: Configuration Flag\\n- Added `use_session_aware_hashes: bool = False` to Settings dataclass\\n- Implemented schema migration and validation tests\\n- Created 9 comprehensive schema tests\\n\\n### Stage 2: Agent Context Integration\\n- Modified AgentManager to generate and track session_id\\n- Updated AgentContext dataclass with session_id field\\n- Integrated session_id propagation through execution context\\n- Created 10 storage integration tests\\n\\n### Stage 3: Hash Function & Tests\\n- Modified `_get_reminder_hash()` in ReminderEngine for session-aware hashing\\n- Updated `ReminderContext` dataclass with session_id field\\n- Added session_id to `_build_variables()` method\\n- Created 5 hash behavior tests with mock.patch approach\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files Modified\\n\\n### Configuration Layer\\n**File**: `config/settings.py`\\n- Added `use_session_aware_hashes` field with default `False`\\n- Maintains frozen dataclass pattern\\n\\n### Agent Management\\n**File**: `execution/agent_manager.py`\\n- Added `session_id` generation in `start_agent_session()`\\n- Updated `AgentContext` dataclass with `session_id: Optional[str]` field\\n- Session IDs propagate through execution context\\n\\n### Reminder Engine\\n**File**: `utils/reminder_engine.py`\\n**Changes**:\\n1. Updated `ReminderContext` dataclass:\\n   ```python\\n   session_id: Optional[str] = None\\n   ```\\n\\n2. Modified `_build_variables()` to include session_id:\\n   ```python\\n   \\\"session_id\\\": context.session_id or \\\"\\\",\\n   ```\\n\\n3. Rewrote `_get_reminder_hash()` with feature flag logic:\\n   ```python\\n   use_session_hash = getattr(settings, 'use_session_aware_hashes', False)\\n   if use_session_hash and session_id:\\n       # Session-aware hash (includes session_id)\\n   else:\\n       # Legacy hash (backward compatible)\\n   ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Tests Created\\n\\n### Stage 1: Schema Tests (`tests/test_reminder_hash_schema.py`)\\n- 9 tests covering settings field, type validation, default values, migration\\n\\n### Stage 2: Storage Tests (`tests/test_reminder_hash_storage.py`)\\n- 10 tests covering session_id propagation, isolation, cleanup, performance\\n\\n### Stage 3: Hash Behavior Tests (`tests/test_reminder_hash_session.py`)\\n- **5 comprehensive tests**:\\n  1. `test_hash_without_session_id` - Legacy format when no session\\n  2. `test_hash_with_session_id_flag_off` - Backward compatibility\\n  3. `test_hash_with_session_id_flag_on` - New behavior validation\\n  4. `test_hash_different_sessions_different_hash` - Session isolation\\n  5. `test_hash_same_session_same_hash` - Hash stability\\n\\n**Test Approach**: Used `unittest.mock.patch` to override frozen Settings dataclass\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test Results Summary\\n\\n### Full Test Suite\\n```\\n32 reminder-related tests: PASSED\\n  - 5 new hash behavior tests\\n  - 9 schema tests\\n  - 10 storage tests\\n  - 8 existing reminder tests\\n\\nOverall: 1024/1051 tests passing\\n  (27 pre-existing failures unrelated to this feature)\\n```\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Hash generation: <1ms per call\\n- No performance regression detected\\n- Memory overhead: Negligible (one UUID string per session)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Implementation Details\\n\\n### Feature Flag Design\\n- **Default OFF**: Ensures zero behavioral change for existing deployments\\n- **Safe activation**: Can be toggled via config without code changes\\n- **getattr fallback**: Graceful handling if flag not present\\n\\n### Backward Compatibility\\n- Legacy hash format preserved when flag is OFF or session_id is None\\n- All existing tests pass without modification\\n- No breaking changes to public APIs\\n\\n### Session Lifecycle\\n```\\nUser Request\\n    \\u2193\\nAgentManager.start_agent_session()\\n    \\u2193 (generates session_id)\\nAgentContext(session_id=\\\"...\\\")\\n    \\u2193\\nReminderContext(session_id=\\\"...\\\")\\n    \\u2193\\n_build_variables() \\u2192 variables[\\\"session_id\\\"]\\n    \\u2193\\n_get_reminder_hash() \\u2192 MD5(session_id project agent tool key)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Edge Cases Handled\\n\\n1. **No session_id provided**: Falls back to legacy hash\\n2. **Feature flag OFF**: Ignores session_id even if present\\n3. **Frozen Settings dataclass**: Tests use mock.patch workaround\\n4. **Empty/None session values**: Treated as empty string (\\\"\\\")\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Performance Benchmarks\\n\\n- **Hash generation**: <1ms (consistent with legacy)\\n- **Test execution**: 0.62s for 5 hash tests\\n- **Full suite**: 22.12s for all 32 reminder tests\\n- **Memory impact**: ~36 bytes per session_id (UUID string)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Confidence Assessment: 0.95\\n\\n**Strengths**:\\n- \\u2705 Comprehensive test coverage (100% of hash paths)\\n- \\u2705 Backward compatibility verified\\n- \\u2705 Feature flag pattern proven safe\\n- \\u2705 All existing tests still pass\\n\\n**Considerations**:\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f Requires manual config change to enable (intentional safety)\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f Session cleanup depends on AgentManager lifecycle\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Follow-Up Recommendations\\n\\n### Immediate (Ready for Review)\\n1. Code review focusing on:\\n   - Hash collision probability\\n   - Session lifecycle edge cases\\n   - Performance under high load\\n\\n### Future Enhancements\\n2. Add session_id to reminder API responses (visibility)\\n3. Consider session-scoped reminder statistics\\n4. Document session isolation behavior in user guide\\n\\n### Monitoring\\n5. Track hash collision rates in production\\n6. Monitor reminder deduplication effectiveness\\n7. Measure session cleanup latency\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nAll Stage 1-3 tasks completed successfully with high confidence. The session-aware reminder hash feature is production-ready with:\\n\", \"line_end\": 200, \"line_start\": 1}, {\"byte_end\": 6084, \"byte_start\": 5835, \"chunk_index\": 1, \"content\": \"- Zero breaking changes\\n- Comprehensive test coverage\\n- Clear migration path (feature flag)\\n- Backward compatibility guarantee\\n\\nReady for mid-implementation review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Generated**: 2026-01-03 18:03 UTC\\n**Agent**: CoderAgent\\n**Confidence**: 95%\\n\", \"line_end\": 212, \"line_start\": 201}], \"frontmatter\": {}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 0, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 0, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"\", \"has_frontmatter\": false, \"mode\": \"chunk\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_tool_output_refinement\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_tool_output_refinement/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT_STAGES_1-3.md\", \"byte_size\": 6084, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 2, \"line_count\": 212, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_tool_output_refinement/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT_STAGES_1-3.md\", \"sha256\": \"21e7efa3e272044544c5ef6f44f820e717a42ded78a9b539adb4ed8e43e46c90\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T18:05:49.163963Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_tool_output_refinement/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T18:05:49.179235+00:00_2ff1c1ca", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T18:05:49.179295+00:00"}
