rations respect normal cooldowns.\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"User requirement states reminders should primarily show on failures, not successes - need to bypass cooldown logic when operation_status='failure'\\\"}\", \"stage\": \"5\", \"task\": \"5.3\"}, \"priority\": \"medium\", \"raw_line\": \"[\\u2705] [2026-01-03 19:14:52 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent] [Project: scribe_tool_output_refinement] Task 5.3 COMPLETED: Implemented failure-priority logic in ReminderEngine._should_show_reminder(). Failures now bypass both cooldowns and teaching session limits.   files=[\\\"utils/reminder_engine.py\\\"]; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Added is_failure flag check at line 325. Wrapped cooldown logic (lines 328-339) in 'if not is_failure' block. Wrapped teaching session limits (lines 342-347) in 'if not is_failure' block. This ensures failures always show reminders regardless of recent history.\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Modified _should_show_reminder() to check is_failure = (context.operation_status == 'failure'). When True, skip cooldown checks and teaching session limits entirely. Success/neutral operations respect normal cooldowns.\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"User requirement states reminders should primarily show on failures, not successes - need to bypass cooldown logic when operation_status='failure'\\\"}; stage=5; task=5.3; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\", \"ts\": \"2026-01-03 19:14:52 UTC\"}, {\"agent\": \"CoderAgent\", \"category\": null, \"confidence\": 1.0, \"emoji\": \"\\u2705\", \"id\": \"6d0a552f53c06668cb4c503dc8cd76d9\", \"message\": \"Task 5.2 COMPLETED: Added operation_status parameter to get_reminders() and ReminderContext. Modified reminders.py (lines 48, 92, 223) and reminder_engine.py (line 57).\", \"meta\": {\"content_type\": \"log\", \"files\": \"[\\\"reminders.py\\\", \\\"utils/reminder_engine.py\\\"]\", \"log_type\": \"progress\", \"priority\": \"medium\", \"reasoning\": \"{\\\"how\\\": \\\"Modified reminders.py to accept operation_status parameter, 