\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u255d\\n\\n\\ud83d\\udcc2 Location:\\n  Root: /home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp\\n  Dev Plan: .scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_tool_output_refinement/\\n\\n\\ud83d\\udcc4 Documents:\\n  \\u2022 ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md (1887 lines)\\n  \\u2022 PHASE_PLAN.md (908 lines)\\n  \\u2022 CHECKLIST.md (598 lines)\\n  \\u2022 PROGRESS_LOG.md (58 entries)\\n\\n\\ud83d\\udcca Recent Activity (last 5 entries):\\n    1. [\\u2139\\ufe0f] 05:08   CoderAgent   Metadata extraction: Production code extracts session_id, project_root, agent_id, tool_name from reminder.variables to pass to storage.record_reminder_shown() with full context tracking   metadata_fields=[\\\"session_id\\\", \\\"project_root\\\", \\\"agent_id\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\", \\\"reminder_key\\\", \\\"operation_status\\\"]; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Used reminder.variables.get() for safe extraction with defaults, context.operation_status for failure priority logic\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Extract 6 metadata fields from reminder.variables and context to pass to DB\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"DB schema requires session_id and metadata for tracking, reminder.variables contains all context\\\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\n    2. [\\u2705] 05:08   CoderAgent   Code reduction: Removed 97 lines of file-based cache code (4 methods + 2 instance variables + config calls), added 34 lines of DB integration code - net reduction of 63 lines   methods_deleted=4; metrics={\\\"lines_added\\\": 34, \\\"lines_removed\\\": 97, \\\"net_reduction\\\": 63}; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"File-based persistence logic replaced with two DB method calls (check_reminder_cooldown, record_reminder_shown)\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Deleted _configure_cooldown_cache, _load_cooldown_cache, _save_cooldown_cache, _cleanup_cooldown_cache plus cache path/dirty tracking\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Simpler codebase with DB handling persistence instead of manual file I/O\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\n    3. [\\u2705] 05:08   CoderAgent   Production entry point: reminders.py _get_engine() modified to create SQLiteStorage from settings.project_root/.scribe/data/scribe.db and inject into engine.storage before returning singleton instance   db_path=settings.project_root/.scribe/data/scribe.db; file=reminders.py; function=_get_engine; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Within if _reminder_engine is None block, create storage before validate_and_load_engine(), then assign to engine.storage\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Added SQLiteStorage import, create storage instance, inject into _reminder_engine.storage\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Production code path must have storage backend to use DB methods instead of files\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\n    4. [\\u2705] 05:08   CoderAgent   Test coverage maintained: 31/31 tests passing including 9 schema tests, 10 storage method tests, 5 hash generation tests, 6 DB activation tests, 1 time variable test - comprehensive validation of DB integration   reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Ran pytest on test_reminder*.py and test_db_activation.py, verified 100% pass rate\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"All test categories pass: table schema, CRUD operations, session isolation, performance, backward compatibility\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Ensure DB integration doesn't break existing functionality and all new features work correctly\\\"}; test_categories={\\\"db_activation\\\": 6, \\\"hash_generation\\\": 5, \\\"schema\\\": 9, \\\"storage_methods\\\": 10, \\\"time_variables\\\": 1}; total_tests=31; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\n    5. [\\u2705] 05:08   CoderAgent   COMMANDMENT #5 compliance achieved: DB infrastructure (table, methods) now fully wired to production code paths. ReminderEngine uses storage.check_reminder_cooldown() and storage.record_reminder_shown() in live code, not just tests.   commandment=5; compliance=complete; evidence=[\\\"storage injection in reminders.py:36\\\", \\\"check_reminder_cooldown in reminder_engine.py:250\\\", \\\"record_reminder_shown in reminder_engine.py:413\\\"]; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Injected storage backend at production entry point, replaced file operations with DB calls, verified with grep\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"All DB methods called from production code paths in _should_show_reminder and generate_reminders\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"User mandate to complete integration in same phase, not leave infrastructure disconnected\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\n\\n\\u23f0 Status: planning   Entries: 775   Last: 2026-01-02 13:48:27.779049+00:00\", \"recent_entries\": [{\"agent\": \"CoderAgent\", \"emoji\": \"\\u2139\\ufe0f\", \"message\": \"Metadata extraction: Production code extracts session_id, project_root, agent_id, tool_name from reminder.variables to pass to storage.record_reminder_shown() with full context tracking   metadata_fields=[\\\"session_id\\\", \\\"project_root\\\", \\\"agent_id\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\", \\\"reminder_key\\\", \\\"operation_status\\\"]; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Used reminder.variables.get() for safe extraction with defaults, context.operation_status for failure priority logic\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Extract 6 metadata fields from reminder.variables and context to pass to DB\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"DB schema requires session_id and metadata for tracking, reminder.variables contains all context\\\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-04 05:08:19 UTC\"}, {\"agent\": \"CoderAgent\", \"emoji\": \"\\u2705\", \"message\": \"Code reduction: Removed 97 lines of file-based cache code (4 methods + 2 instance variables + config calls), added 34 lines of DB integration code - net reduction of 63 lines   methods_deleted=4; metrics={\\\"lines_added\\\": 34, \\\"lines_removed\\\": 97, \\\"net_reduction\\\": 63}; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"File-based persistence logic replaced with two DB method calls (check_remind